					<description><![CDATA[<p>AI Customer Experience Platform Attracts New Investment Omilia announced closing a $67 million Series B funding round supporting expansion of its AI-powered customer experience platform. Expedition Growth Capital led the</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/omilia-secures-67m-series-b-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal">Omilia Secures $67M To Expand AI Customer Experience Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>AI Customer Experience Platform Attracts New Investment</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Omilia announced closing a $67 million Series B funding round supporting expansion of its AI-powered customer experience platform. Expedition Growth Capital led the investment, marking the company&#8217;s second institutional funding round since its founding.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The funding will accelerate global expansion, particularly across North America, while strengthening commercial operations and market presence. Omilia will also reinforce its senior management team while advancing its voice artificial intelligence technology capabilities.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Omilia provides AI-driven customer service solutions for large enterprises operating in sectors such as banking, insurance and healthcare. Its customers include Capital One, Discover, RBC, Taco Bell, DWP and PSEG.</span></p>
<h2><b>Funding Supports Enterprise AI Expansion</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Opmilia adds the company says demand is only increasing for enterprise-ready AI powered by a fully automated solution that is designed to provide scalable and intelligent CX and that does not comprise security, compliant costs or that can support costs coming into the office. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Rather than most third party LLM based solutions the voice-based AI has Opmilia’s own developed proprietary voice AI technology. This allows enterprises to deploy high-volume customer interactions while maintaining low latency, transparent pricing and greater operational control.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Dimitris Vassos said the company&#8217;s cloud platform has become a critical part of daily customer interactions for many global enterprises. The latest investment would accelerate the rollout of Omilia&#8217;s self-learning AI agents to organisations seeking modern contact centre technology.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Omilia has increased its annual recurring revenue by more than tenfold to over $60 million. The company attributed its growth to rising adoption of its Self-Learning Agentic CX platform and pricing models that eliminate unpredictable token-based costs.</span></p>
<h2><b>Platform Adoption Continues Across Large Enterprises<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_204115" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-204115" class="size-full wp-image-204115" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/a-futuristic-poster-showcases-a-sprawlin_eTrqIltBXf2Li1iqgQiYDw_BgjLxtzJSQS83cIelRcbLQ_cover.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing AI voice systems handling large-scale customer interactions." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-204115" class="wp-caption-text">Omilia powers enterprise-scale AI voice platforms for automated and compliant customer engagement. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Omilia currently powers some of the largest AI voice deployments in production. These include a major US bank handling more than one million calls daily and an insurance provider processing over 600,000 agent-assisted interactions every day.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The platform is designed to support regulated industries that require strict compliance standards, including FedRAMP, PCI-DSS, SOC 2, HIPAA and GDPR. In contrast with a purely generative AI based strategy, it blends tailored AI capabilities.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company recently expanded its partnership with Taco Bell, where its voice AI technology now supports ordering across more than 1,000 drive-thru locations in 38 US states. Omilia also introduced Lexis, a generative text-to-speech model built specifically for enterprise contact centres.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Expedition Growth Capital Founder and Managing Partner Oliver Thomas said Omilia combines deep industry expertise with proven product leadership. He noted that its self-learning customer experience platform delivers measurable operational improvements while maintaining transparency and </span><a href="https://dealhub.io/glossary/predictable-costs/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">predictable costs</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400">.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: <a href="https://ventureburn.com/moss-raises-30-million-series-c/" data-wpel-link="internal">Moss Raises €30 Million To Reach Unicorn Status</a></span></p>
<h2><b>New Capital Targets Global Growth And Product Development</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The fresh funding will finance Omilia&#8217;s first US office, scheduled to open later this year. It would also include a range of new commercial recruits in leadership positions, from those focused on revenue to more specialised roles covering marketing and international growth. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company anticipates an expansion in the workforce size from approximately 500 to about 600 by year-end. Omilia said it intends to stay focused on helping organisations automate conversational interfaces, while enabling human service agents to deal with higher complexity.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Given the ongoing drive for businesses for conversational and AI driven support, Omilia said its strategy will enable it to secure deeper relationships with companies across financials, healthcare, retail and regulated sectors.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
