					<description><![CDATA[<p>Funding Accelerates Finance AI Platform Expansion  Berlin-based Fintech Moss has secured 30 million (25 million pounds) in Series C funding, bringing it to unicorn status with a valuation exceeding 1</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/moss-raises-30-million-series-c/" data-wpel-link="internal">Moss Raises €30 Million To Reach Unicorn Status</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Funding Accelerates Finance AI Platform Expansion</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> </span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Berlin-based Fintech Moss has secured 30 million (25 million pounds) in Series C funding, bringing it to unicorn status with a </span><a href="https://www.investopedia.com/terms/v/valuation.asp" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">valuation</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> exceeding 1 billion. The latest funding will accelerate development of Moss&#8217; Finance AI platform for European business customers significantly.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Moss will also expand digital spend management services for small and medium-sized enterprises across Europe successfully. Portage led the Series C, while previous investor Cherry Ventures was also part of the round. Moss&#8217;s funding now exceeds 160 million in total since its establishment in 2019.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">This news comes as companies begin to embrace AI to ease financial tasks, and improve decision-making. It is thought that there will be further growth for solutions that combine automation and human input to make finances more efficient without negatively impacting accuracy or compliance.</span></p>
<h2><b>Moss Expands Finance AI Platform</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Moss plans to use the new capital to move beyond traditional spend management by building a broader suite of artificial intelligence tools for finance teams. The company is developing configurable AI agents capable of supporting finance professionals with routine operational tasks while ensuring that final business decisions remain under human control.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Rather than allowing AI to make autonomous financial decisions, Moss has designed its platform to prepare work, explain every recommendation, and require user approval before executing important actions.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Chief Executive Officer and co-founder Ante Spittler said the company&#8217;s next phase will focus on delivering AI that improves productivity while preserving transparency and accountability throughout financial workflows.</span></p>
<h2><b>Spend Management Platform Gains Strong Adoption</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Established by Ante Spittler, Anton Rummel, Ferdinand Meyer and Stephan Haslebacher back in 2019 Moss supplies companies with an all-in-one solution spend management that simplifies a department’s core financial tasks.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The platform&#8217;s software solution bundles corporate payment cards, invoice processing, employee expenses and accounting and the real-time management and budgeting of the latter in one place. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Moss relies on intelligent AI agents which automatically categorize and balance transactions reducing labor-intensive manual reconciliation at closing period as it states more than two million transactions currently processed monthly by the company. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Over 5,000 business companies in the UK, the Netherlands, Germany and Austria use the software of Moss, which achieved more than €70 million annual recurring revenue while growth still comes in at around 65 percent.</span></p>
<h2><b>AI Strategy Prioritises Human Oversight<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_204110" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-204110" class="size-full wp-image-204110" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/a-futuristic-poster-showcases-an-ai-powe_RnODeiC0WhemwPnY4LG3XA_GnzmNEIrStuvDIhnuOJhAQ_cover.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing AI assisting finance professionals with controlled decision-making." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-204110" class="wp-caption-text">Moss emphasises human-controlled AI to enhance trust and efficiency in financial operations. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Artificial intelligence is becoming the centrepiece of Moss&#8217; long-term product strategy. The company believes this human-in-the-loop approach will improve trust while allowing organisations to benefit from faster financial operations.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Unlike some competing financial software providers, Moss believes finance teams should retain complete authority over important decisions. Its AI is designed to assist rather than replace finance professionals.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company&#8217;s research supports that approach. In a survey commissioned by Moss involving 471 finance leaders, nearly half identified control as the most important factor when adopting AI-powered finance tools, while only a small minority preferred fully autonomous systems.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: <a href="https://ventureburn.com/healthsnap-secures-25-million-growth-financing/" data-wpel-link="internal">HealthSnap Secures $25M To Expand AI-Powered Virtual Care Platform</a></span></p>
<h2><b>Funding Strengthens European Expansion</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The latest funding positions Moss to strengthen its presence across Europe&#8217;s growing financial technology market. The company currently operates from Berlin, with additional offices in Tallinn and Amsterdam, employing around 339 people.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Moss competes with several global spend management platforms but believes its emphasis on explainable AI and human oversight provides a meaningful competitive advantage as finance departments increasingly adopt automation.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/moss-raises-30-million-series-c/" data-wpel-link="internal">Moss Raises €30 Million To Reach Unicorn Status</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
